### Area of Improvement

Let's stop overusing destructuring. We do this in the docs and probably in the codebase too.

I'm going to quote myself (like a twat, haha): 
> If you only use a prop once, all you're doing by destructing it is to add extra code, make discoverability of what else is on the object harder and add indirection on where the variable comes from.
>
> — https://twitter.com/alexdotjs/status/1635012632116854784

That said, most of these examples are because of me, so no one else to blame here than yours truly :D

 

General rule of thumb:

- Destructuring in function arguments is not ok
- Destructuring in body is ok
- Don't destruct a prop if it's only used once

