Express allows me to define middleware per route:
https://expressjs.com/en/guide/using-middleware.html#middleware.router
while tRPC effectively only allows you to attach middleware to the router.

I'd love to be able to do something like this:
```typescript
export const dogRouter = createRouter()  
  .query("getDog", {
    input: GetDogInput,
    middleware: [GetAuthorizerMiddleware("READ", "Dog")],
    resolve({ input }) {
      return getDog(input.id);
    },
  })
  .query("createDog", {
    input: CreateDogInput,
    middleware: [GetAuthorizerMiddleware("WRITE", "Dog")],
    resolve({ input }) {
      return createDog(input);
    },
  });
```

Currently I'd need to put the middleware evaluation logic in the `resolve` function.
